    "https://careers.cccu.org/job/assistant-professor-english-department-9-mo-tt-birmingham-alabama-12610": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, English Department (9 Mo, TT)",
      "description": "Assistant Professor, English Department (9 Mo, TT) in Birmingham, Alabama | Council for Christian Colleges and Universities Home Search Directory Contact Us Career Resources Career Advice Interview Coach Offer Analyzer Pricing Register Job Seekers Employers Sign In Post a Job Assistant Professor, English Department (9 Mo, TT) Samford University Birmingham, Alabama Share Save Job Apply for This Job ASSISTANT PROFESSOR, ENGLISH DEPARTMENT (9-month, Tenure-Track Appointment) September 2, 2026 Samford University’s Howard College of Arts and Sciences invites individuals interested in serving in a Christian university environment to submit applications for a position as Assistant Professor of English, beginning August 2027. We seek a writer of fiction and/or nonfiction with secondary expertise in digital literacies, technologies of writing and research, and/or multimodal composition. This tenure-track position carries a twenty-four (24) credit hour teaching load per academic year, as well as expectations for active research and service. Teaching will include advanced and introductory courses for the Department and first-year writing courses for the General Education program. A robust and realistic scholarly agenda is expected, as is service to department, college, university, and community initiatives. Qualified candidates must hold an M FA in creative writing and/or a PhD or ABD, near completion, in English ; have a publication record as a writer of fiction or nonfiction; and be prepared to equip students to navigate the current digital landscape and utilize emerging technologies and AI. Applicants with secondary expertise in digital studies, digital literacies, and/or digital media are encouraged to apply. Applicants with training and experience teaching first-year writing are also encouraged to apply. Successful candidates will be committed to excellent teaching, student development and mentorship, and collegial collaboration. ABD candidates will be hired at the rank of Instructor, with a commensurate salary, until Ph.D. is completed. English studies has been a central focus of Samford University since the university’s founding in 1841, when the original institution was called the Howard College of English and Classical Studies. Fourteen faculty members serve approximately sixty majors in a traditional BA program of writing and literary study, in optional concentrations in Writing and Film, and minors in English, Film and Video Studies, and Writing. The department supports a master’s degree program in Samford’s Orlean Beeson School of Education and cooperates with Samford University’s 3-3 program in the Cumberland School of Law. For more information, see Samford’s English Department here . Located in the Homewood suburb of Birmingham, Alabama, Samford ( samford.edu ) is a leading Christian university offering undergraduate programs grounded in the liberal arts with an array of nationally recognized graduate and professional schools. Founded in 1841, Samford enrolls 6,324 students from 44 states, Puerto Rico and 16 countries in its 10 academic schools with 450 full-time faculty. Samford is ranked #3 in the nation for career preparation and #8 in the nation for student learning opportunities as listed in The Wall Street Journal (2026). The University is dedicated to the promotion of rigorous academic inquiry in a Christian setting. The University seeks and prefers employee applicants of the Christian faith and offers competitive salaries with a generous benefits package. Review of applications will begin November 15, 2026, and applications will be accepted until January 15, 2027. Please submit the following documents: 1) an application letter that includes statement of teaching philosophy and experience and a description of research interests and activities, 2) a curriculum vitae with contact information for three references, 3) an application for faculty position, and 4) the faculty applicant Christian mission statement. (The application and the statement are available at the links below.) Salary is dependent upon qualifications and experience. The successful candidate must pass a background check. Applicants must be authorized to work in the United States, as Samford will not sponsor any employment visa for this position. “Application for Faculty Position” can be found at: https://www.samford.edu/departments/files/Human_Resources/application-for-faculty-employment.pdf “Faculty Applicant Christian Mission Statement” can be found at: https://www.samford.edu/departments/files/academic-affairs/Faculty-Applicant-Christian-Mission-Statement.docx Please submit all materials in PDF format to: [email protected] Subject : Asst. Prof., English Questions may be addressed to the search committee chair, Dr. Brad Busbee ( [email protected] ). In accordance with applicable federal and state laws, such as Titles VI and VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, the Age Discrimination in Employment Act, and the Americans with Disabilities Act and ADA Amendments, the University does not unlawfully discriminate on the basis of sex, gender, race, color, national origin, age, disability, genetic information, veteran status, religion, or any other protected status under federal, state or local law applicable to the University, in its education policies, programs, and activities, in its admissions policies, in employment policies and practices, and all other areas of the University. As a faith-based institution, the University is exempted from certain laws and regulations concerning discrimination. Job Information Job Category: Faculty Careers - English Literature and Composition Position Type: Full Time Related Jobs Faculty, Clinical Psychology - College of Education and Behavioral Sciences Azusa Pacific University Azusa, California Posted - August 27, 2026 View Virginia and Tom Williams Endowed Chair of American Literature, Department of English, Associate Professor or Professor Baylor University Waco, Texas Posted - July 15, 2026 View Tenure-track, Open-rank English Faculty Mississippi Christian University Clinton, Mississippi Posted - September 3, 2026 View Religion Faculty Calvin University Grand Rapids, Michigan Posted - September 4, 2026 View Nursing - Assistant Professor Hope College Holland, Michigan Posted - September 4, 2026 View Assistant/Associate Professor of History LeTourneau University Longview, Texas Posted - September 3, 2026 View Show More Jobs Trending Job Titles Associate Professor of Finance Nursing Assistant Professor Trending Locations Iowa California Oregon Minnesota Birmingham, Alabama Houston, Texas Azusa, California Florida Alabama Illinois West Palm Beach, Florida Indiana Grand Rapids, Michigan Michigan Cedarville, Ohio Anderson, Indiana St. Paul, Minnesota Portland, Oregon Texas Virginia ORANGE CITY, Iowa Virginia Beach, Virginia Ohio Longview, Texas Wheaton, Illinois Trending Companies Regent University Azusa Pacific University LeTourneau University Palm Beach Atlantic University Cedarville University Samford University Houston Christian University Northwestern College Calvin University Wheaton College Trending Categories Faculty Careers - Psychology Faculty Careers - Business Faculty Careers - Religion Faculty Careers - Communication/Design/Media Faculty Careers - Education Faculty Careers - Biology/Life Sciences Faculty Careers - Engineering Faculty Careers - Chemistry/Biochemistry Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Development/Fundraising Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Other Education Faculty Careers - Health Professions Apply for this job Find Jobs By Category Education Faculty Careers - Health Professions Faculty Careers - Biology/Life Sciences Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Other Faculty Careers - Psychology Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Development/Fundraising Faculty Careers - Engineering Faculty Careers - Communication/Design/Media Faculty Careers - Religion Faculty Careers - Chemistry/Biochemistry Powered by Web Scribble Solutions , Inc. About Our Work & Mission Our Institutions Leadership Contact Us Join Us Advertise Donate Employment Membership Sponsorship Follow Us Council for Christian Colleges & Universities 20 M Street SE, Suite 350 , Washington, D.C. 20003 202.546.8713"
    },
    "https://careers.cccu.org/job/nursing-assistant-professor-holland-michigan-12615": {
      "title": "Nursing - Assistant Professor",
      "description": "Nursing - Assistant Professor in Holland, Michigan | Council for Christian Colleges and Universities Home Search Directory Contact Us Career Resources Career Advice Interview Coach Offer Analyzer Pricing Register Job Seekers Employers Sign In Post a Job Nursing - Assistant Professor Hope College Holland, Michigan Share Save Job Apply for This Job Position Title Nursing - Assistant Professor Classification Title Faculty Full Time (.75-1.0 FTE) Benefits Eligibility Benefits Eligibility Department Nursing Job Description Hope College invites applications for a tenure-track faculty position in the Department of Nursing. The successful candidate will primarily teach undergraduate nursing courses in nursing research, adult health (medical-surgical) nursing, and other BSN courses as assigned. Teaching responsibilities may include classroom, laboratory, clinical, and practicum instruction. Responsibilities include: Developing and delivering high-quality instruction; Designing, administering, and evaluating student learning experiences and assessments; Supervising students in clinical and practicum settings; Advising and mentoring students academically and professionally; Contributing to curriculum development, program assessment, and continuous quality improvement. Faculty are expected to maintain an active program of scholarship, engage in ongoing professional development, and provide service to the department, college, and profession consistent with the expectations of a tenure-track appointment at Hope College. Is this a visiting faculty position? No Rank Assistant Qualifications Required Qualifications Current or eligible for registered nurse licensure in the State of Michigan. Demonstrated expertise in adult health (medical-surgical) nursing. Evidence of effective teaching or clinical education. Strong communication, collaboration, and mentoring skills. Earned PhD in Nursing or a closely related nursing terminal degree by the time of appointment. Candidates who are All But Dissertation (ABD) and are expected to complete the doctoral degree by the date of appointment or within one year of hire are encouraged to apply. Successful applicants will demonstrate a commitment to all aspects of Hope’s mission as a liberal arts college. Hope College is grounded in robust ecumenical Christian aspirations and strives for inclusive excellence. As part of the application, we ask all candidates to describe how they will engage with and support the holistic mission of the College, particularly how their Christian faith, commitment to the liberal arts, and inclusive excellence shape their work as teachers, scholars, and mentors. More guidelines for Hope College candidate’s response to the mission statement can be found at hope.edu/jobs . Preferred Qualifications Experience teaching undergraduate nursing research, evidence-based practice, and adult health (medical-surgical) nursing. Experience supervising undergraduate research, evidence-based practice, or capstone/practicum projects. Demonstrated record of scholarly activity with the potential to establish and sustain a program of scholarship consistent with tenure expectations. Commitment to student-centered teaching and mentoring within a liberal arts environment. Physical Demands This position requires remaining in a sitting or standing position for frequent periods of time; uses office machinery such as a computers, printers, copy machines; Occasionally involves moving items over 10 pounds; frequently will move between different offices/workspaces/buildings; and requires effective communication abilities. In the case of temporary or permanent condition(s) that require(s) accommodation(s), reasonable accommodation(s) may be requested. Pre-employment Screenings “All offers of employment are contingent upon a background check. Some positions may have position specific requirements, such as education/licensure/certification verification, a physical, drug screening, credit checks and/or transportation record review.” Posting Detail Information Posting Number 2026-004FR Job Posting Open Date 08/04/2026 Job Posting Close Date 09/20/2026 Open Until Filled No Is this position available for sponsorship No Special Instructions to Applicants Quick Link for Internal Postings https://jobs.hope.edu/postings/5512 Job Information Job Category: Nurse Education: Doctorate Degree Experience: 5 - 10 years Related Jobs Assistant/Associate Professor of Nursing, Undergraduate Program - Community Nursing Palm Beach Atlantic University West Palm Beach, Florida Posted - August 21, 2026 View Director, The Center for Academic MInistry LeTourneau University Longview, Texas Posted - August 21, 2026 View Assistant/Associate Professor of Nursing Crown College Saint Bonifacius, Minnesota Posted - September 1, 2026 View Assistant or Associate Professor of Accounting LeTourneau University Longview, Texas Posted - August 21, 2026 View Assistant/Associate Professor of Nursing, Undergraduate Program - Pediatrics Palm Beach Atlantic University West Palm Beach, Florida Posted - August 21, 2026 View Assistant/Associate Professor of History LeTourneau University Longview, Texas Posted - September 3, 2026 View Show More Jobs Trending Job Titles Associate Professor of Finance Nursing Assistant Professor Trending Locations Virginia Beach, Virginia Grand Rapids, Michigan Indiana ORANGE CITY, Iowa Cedarville, Ohio Ohio Oregon Birmingham, Alabama Longview, Texas Wheaton, Illinois Portland, Oregon Houston, Texas Illinois Florida Alabama St. Paul, Minnesota California Virginia Minnesota Michigan West Palm Beach, Florida Iowa Texas Azusa, California Anderson, Indiana Trending Companies Palm Beach Atlantic University LeTourneau University Regent University Samford University Cedarville University Calvin University Azusa Pacific University Northwestern College Wheaton College Houston Christian University Trending Categories Faculty Careers - Psychology Faculty Careers - Communication/