    "https://careers.cccu.org/job/assistant-professor-of-public-relations-department-of-communication-and-media-9-mo-tt-birmingham-alabama-12612": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Public Relations, Department of Communication and Media (9 Mo, TT)",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Public Relations, Department of Communication and Media (9 Mo, TT) in Birmingham, Alabama | Council for Christian Colleges and Universities Home Search Directory Contact Us Career Resources Career Advice Interview Coach Offer Analyzer Pricing Register Job Seekers Employers Sign In Post a Job Assistant Professor of Public Relations, Department of Communication and Media (9 Mo, TT) Samford University Birmingham, Alabama Share Save Job Apply for This Job Assistant Professor of Public Relations Department of Communication and Media (9-month appointment, Tenure Track) September 2, 2026 Samford University’s Howard College of Arts and Sciences invites individuals interested in serving in a Christian University environment to apply for an Assistant Professor of Public Relations position in the Department of Communication and Media. This full-time tenure track position is a 9-month appointment and carries a twenty-four (24) credit-hour teaching load. The position will begin in August 2027. Qualified candidates will hold a Ph.D. or be ABD, near completion, in mass communication, communication, or a closely related field from an institutionally accredited college or university (or equivalent). Candidates with relevant professional experience and ability to teach a variety of public relations courses including principles of public relations, public relations writing, and public relations campaigns are preferred. Additional expertise in brand and content strategy, and/or strategic communication, advertising and content creation a plus. Successful candidates will have demonstrated a record of peer-reviewed scholarship and excellence in teaching. ABD candidates will be considered at the rank of Instructor, with commensurate salary, until Ph.D. is completed. The Department of Communication and Media is home to Samford’s award-winning student media and hosts an annual speaker forum (Robinson Forum - a lecture series in cooperation with The Washington Post). Our Public Relations program is CEPR certified. Located in the Homewood suburb of Birmingham, Alabama, Samford (samford.edu) is a leading Christian university offering undergraduate programs grounded in the liberal arts with an array of nationally recognized graduate and professional schools. Founded in 1841, Samford enrolls 6,324 students from 44 states, Puerto Rico and 16 countries in its 10 academic schools with 450 full-time faculty. Samford is ranked #3 in the nation for career preparation and #8 in the nation for student learning opportunities as listed in The Wall Street Journal (2026). The University is dedicated to the promotion of rigorous academic inquiry in a Christian setting. The University seeks and prefers employee applicants of the Christian faith and offers competitive salaries with a generous benefits package. Review of applications will begin October 9, 2026, and applications will continue to be accepted until October 23, 2026. Please submit (via email below in .pdf format), an application letter, curriculum vitae with names and contact information of three references, description of teaching experience and interests, description of research plans, along with an Application for Faculty Position and the Faculty Applicant Christian Mission Statement (links below). Salary is dependent upon qualifications and experience. The successful candidate must pass a background check. Applicants must be authorized to work in the United States, as Samford will not sponsor any employment visas for this position. Application for Faculty Position can be found at: https://www.samford.edu/departments/files/Human_Resources/application-for-faculty-employment.pdf Faculty Applicant Christian Mission Statement can be found at: https://www.samford.edu/departments/files/academic-affairs/Faculty-Applicant-Christian-Mission-Statement.docx Please submit all materials in PDF format to: [email protected] Subject: Public Relations Faculty Questions may be addressed to: Dr. Ignatius Fosu, Search Committee Chair [email protected] In accordance with applicable federal and state laws, such as Titles VI and VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, the Age Discrimination in Employment Act, and the Americans with Disabilities Act and ADA Amendments, the University does not unlawfully discriminate on the basis of sex, gender, race, color, national origin, age, disability, genetic information, veteran status, religion, or any other protected status under federal, state or local law applicable to the University, in its education policies, programs, and activities, in its admissions policies, in employment policies and practices, and all other areas of the University. As a faith-based institution, the University is exempted from certain laws and regulations concerning discrimination. Job Information Job Category: Faculty Careers - Communication/ Design/ Media Position Type: Full Time Related Jobs Assistant Professor, Department of Communication and Media (9 Mo, TT) Samford University Birmingham, Alabama Posted - September 3, 2026 View Assistant/Associate Professor of Finance Grace College & Seminary Winona Lake, Indiana Posted - April 29, 2026 View Tenure-track, Open-rank English Faculty Mississippi Christian University Clinton, Mississippi Posted - September 3, 2026 View Assistant Professor, English Department (9 Mo, TT) Samford University Birmingham, Alabama Posted - September 3, 2026 View Religion Faculty Calvin University Grand Rapids, Michigan Posted - September 4, 2026 View Assistant/Associate Professor of History LeTourneau University Longview, Texas Posted - September 3, 2026 View Show More Jobs Trending Job Titles Associate Professor of Finance Nursing Assistant Professor Trending Locations Florida Grand Rapids, Michigan Virginia Azusa, California Michigan Texas Minnesota Ohio Longview, Texas Illinois ORANGE CITY, Iowa St. Paul, Minnesota Alabama Portland, Oregon Houston, Texas Cedarville, Ohio Oregon Wheaton, Illinois Iowa West Palm Beach, Florida California Anderson, Indiana Birmingham, Alabama Indiana Virginia Beach, Virginia Trending Companies Calvin University Cedarville University Northwestern College Azusa Pacific University LeTourneau University Houston Christian University Regent University Wheaton College Palm Beach Atlantic University Samford University Trending Categories Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Other Education Faculty Careers - Health Professions Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Development/Fundraising Faculty Careers - Communication/Design/Media Faculty Careers - Biology/Life Sciences Faculty Careers - Engineering Faculty Careers - Psychology Faculty Careers - Education Faculty Careers - Business Faculty Careers - Religion Faculty Careers - Chemistry/Biochemistry Apply for this job Find Jobs By Category Education Faculty Careers - Health Professions Faculty Careers - Biology/Life Sciences Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Other Faculty Careers - Psychology Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Development/Fundraising Faculty Careers - Engineering Faculty Careers - Communication/Design/Media Faculty Careers - Religion Faculty Careers - Chemistry/Biochemistry Powered by Web Scribble Solutions , Inc. About Our Work & Mission Our Institutions Leadership Contact Us Join Us Advertise Donate Employment Membership Sponsorship Follow Us Council for Christian Colleges & Universities 20 M Street SE, Suite 350 , Washington, D.C. 20003 202.546.8713"
