    "https://careers.cccu.org/job/tenure-track-open-rank-english-faculty-clinton-mississippi-12609": {
      "title": "Tenure-track, Open-rank English Faculty",
      "description": "Tenure-track, Open-rank English Faculty in Clinton, Mississippi | Council for Christian Colleges and Universities Home Search Directory Contact Us Career Resources Career Advice Interview Coach Offer Analyzer Pricing Register Job Seekers Employers Sign In Post a Job Tenure-track, Open-rank English Faculty Mississippi Christian University Clinton, Mississippi Share Save Job Apply for This Job Job Summary The Department of English and World Languages at Mississippi Christian University invites applications for a tenure-track, open-rank English faculty position beginning Fall 2027. We welcome applicants with the ability to teach a variety of generalist literature and writing courses. We also encourage applications from candidates whose areas of specialization will expand the breadth and variety of courses offered. Candidates should demonstrate enthusiasm for teaching undergraduate and graduate English courses as well as a willingness to support the department’s emphasis on a systematic, methods-driven approach to textual analysis. The ideal candidate will join a supportive and collaborative department dedicated to the needs of students, the mission of the department, and the mission of the university. Job Duties Teach four courses per semester, a combination of core curriculum and upper level courses Support, mentor, and advise students Contribute to ongoing strategic planning for the future of the department within the School of Christian Studies, Humanities and the Arts Keep a minimum of ten in-person office hours per week during each semester Serve on departmental and university committees Support Mississippi Christian University’s mission Minimum Qualifications Applicants must have a terminal degree in English or closely related field in hand before the start date of the appointment. To be considered, applicants must complete the Mississippi Christian University employment application and submit a letter of application, CV, and statement of teaching philosophy to [email protected] or Dr. David Miller, English Professor Search Committee, Box 4022, Mississippi Christian University, Clinton, MS  39058. Review of applications will begin on 12 November 2026. Transcripts and letters of recommendation will be requested after initial screenings. Shortlisted candidates will be invited to interview in early 2027. About the Department The Department of English and World Languages offers courses in literature, language, linguistics, cultural studies, textual analysis, qualitative research, English secondary education, and philosophy. Courses emphasize the exploration and production of a variety of texts in various modes with careful attention to replicable methodologies. The department also supports several minors: English studies for non-majors, applied humanities, African American studies, and philosophy. About the University Mississippi Christian University, with more than 80 undergraduate majors and 50 graduate areas of study, values its reputation for academic excellence and its commitment to the integration of faith and learning. Mississippi Christian University is a private comprehensive institution affiliated with the Mississippi Baptist Convention; it actively seeks faculty and staff who are committed Christians and whose Christian principles are exemplified in daily living. Job Information Job Category: Faculty Careers - English Literature and Composition Education: Doctorate Degree Experience: Entry Level Position Type: Full Time Related Jobs Virginia and Tom Williams Endowed Chair of American Literature, Department of English, Associate Professor or Professor Baylor University Waco, Texas Posted - July 15, 2026 View ECE Program Director/Faculty (Early Childhood Education, Early Literacy, Early Math), Teacher Education Azusa Pacific University Azusa, California Posted - August 27, 2026 View Faculty, Clinical Psychology - College of Education and Behavioral Sciences Azusa Pacific University Azusa, California Posted - August 27, 2026 View Assistant Professor, English Department (9 Mo, TT) Samford University Birmingham, Alabama Posted - September 3, 2026 View Nursing - Assistant Professor Hope College Holland, Michigan Posted - September 4, 2026 View Religion Faculty Calvin University Grand Rapids, Michigan Posted - September 4, 2026 View Show More Jobs Trending Job Titles Nursing Assistant Professor Associate Professor of Finance Trending Locations Oregon Virginia Virginia Beach, Virginia Azusa, California Illinois Houston, Texas Ohio Michigan Florida Wheaton, Illinois Anderson, Indiana Texas St. Paul, Minnesota Birmingham, Alabama Iowa Indiana West Palm Beach, Florida Alabama Grand Rapids, Michigan ORANGE CITY, Iowa Portland, Oregon Minnesota Longview, Texas California Cedarville, Ohio Trending Companies Cedarville University Azusa Pacific University LeTourneau University Palm Beach Atlantic University Houston Christian University Northwestern College Calvin University Wheaton College Regent University Samford University Trending Categories Faculty Careers - Communication/Design/Media Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Development/Fundraising Faculty Careers - Religion Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Other Faculty Careers - Business Faculty Careers - Engineering Faculty Careers - Education Faculty Careers - Health Professions Faculty Careers - Biology/Life Sciences Faculty Careers - Psychology Faculty Careers - Chemistry/Biochemistry Education Apply for this job Find Jobs By Category Education Faculty Careers - Health Professions Faculty Careers - Biology/Life Sciences Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Other Faculty Careers - Psychology Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Development/Fundraising Faculty Careers - Engineering Faculty Careers - Communication/Design/Media Faculty Careers - Religion Faculty Careers - Chemistry/Biochemistry Powered by Web Scribble Solutions , Inc. About Our Work & Mission Our Institutions Leadership Contact Us Join Us Advertise Donate Employment Membership Sponsorship Follow Us Council for Christian Colleges & Universities 20 M Street SE, Suite 350 , Washington, D.C. 20003 202.546.8713"
