    "https://careers.cccu.org/job/assistant-associate-or-full-professor-of-language-and-literacy-education-wenham-massachusetts-12608": {
      "title": "Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor of Language and Literacy Education",
      "description": "Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor of Language and Literacy Education in Wenham, Massachusetts | Council for Christian Colleges and Universities Home Search Directory Contact Us Career Resources Career Advice Interview Coach Offer Analyzer Pricing Register Job Seekers Employers Sign In Post a Job Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor of Language and Literacy Education Gordon College Wenham, Massachusetts Share Save Job Apply for This Job The Herschend School of Education at Gordon College invites applications for a full time tenure track faculty position at the rank of assistant, associate, or full professor to teach in an Ed.D. program in the Science of Learning with emphasis on Language and Literacy Education. This is a primarily online program with an annual one week residential summer institute. Position to begin May or August 2027. Rank will be commensurate with experience. Gordon College is a Christian liberal arts college located in Massachusetts on Boston’s North Shore, a beautiful coastal area with easy access to Boston. This Ed.D. builds on the Herschend School’s thirty year history of rigorous graduate education programs grounded in evidence-based practices to equip all children to learn to read proficiently. Our graduate reading specialist program has the distinction of the “accreditation plus” rating by the International Dyslexia Association. We seek faculty excited to build on this legacy in a CPED-aligned doctoral program aiming to graduate scholar-practitioners ready to serve as the next generation of leaders, changeagents, problem solvers, and advocates within K-12 education, speech-language pathology clinical practice, education policy, and educator/SLP preparation. Responsibilities: • Teach online graduate courses and participate in annual residential summer institute; Depending on expertise, possible option to also teach in person undergraduate courses. • Advise students, supporting the full student experience, including timely degree completion; • Participate in and chair dissertation committees; • Serve on the admissions committee, collaborating to screen applicants and select new cohort members; • Engage in research and scholarly activities, including seeking grant funding and fostering external partnerships; • Engage in purposeful service to the institution and the profession. Qualifications of the Ideal Candidate: • A commitment to the Christian mission of the college; • Earned doctorate in education, speech-language pathology, cognitive psychology, or a closely related field; • Expertise in the science of learning, language and literacy education, instructional leadership, and/or research methods; • Commitment to evidence-based practices to equitably support all learners, including culturally and linguistically sustaining practices; • Three or more years of experience with K-12 teaching/tutoring, SLP clinical practice, or applied research; • Evidence of effective teaching, with preference for experience teaching in online settings; • Demonstrated leadership in education or clinical settings; • Active research program with potential for student collaboration; • Passion for mentoring aspiring literacy leaders; • Strong interpersonal skills with ability to communicate and collaborate with faculty, staff, and students. Interested Applicants Must Submit: • Cover letter that addresses the applicant’s fit with the Christian mission of Gordon College and a rationale for interest in this specific position; • CV that includes the names and contact information for 3 references; • A sample of academic writing. Anticipated Salary Range: $64,733 - $97,300 commensurate with experience. TO APPLY: https://www.gordon.edu/offices-services/human-resources/jobs/open-facultypositions#full-time Visit https://www.gordon.edu/offices-services/human-resources/for-prospective-employees for more information on Gordon College. Our review of applicants will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Gordon College is an equal opportunity employer. Qualified applicants for employment will receive consideration without discrimination on the basis of race, color, gender, age, national origin, or disability. Job Information Job Category: Faculty Careers - Education Salary: $64,733 - $97,300 Per Year Education: Doctorate Degree Experience: 10 - 20 years Position Type: Full Time Related Jobs Assistant Professor, English Department (9 Mo, TT) Samford University Birmingham, Alabama Posted - September 3, 2026 View Assistant Professor of Public Relations, Department of Communication and Media (9 Mo, TT) Samford University Birmingham, Alabama Posted - September 3, 2026 View Nursing - Assistant Professor Hope College Holland, Michigan Posted - September 4, 2026 View Assistant/Associate Professor of History LeTourneau University Longview, Texas Posted - September 3, 2026 View Religion Faculty Calvin University Grand Rapids, Michigan Posted - September 4, 2026 View Assistant Professor, Department of Communication and Media (9 Mo, TT) Samford University Birmingham, Alabama Posted - September 3, 2026 View Show More Jobs Trending Job Titles Nursing Assistant Professor Associate Professor of Finance Trending Locations Florida West Palm Beach, Florida ORANGE CITY, Iowa Minnesota Iowa Alabama Birmingham, Alabama Longview, Texas Indiana Azusa, California Portland, Oregon Houston, Texas Texas Cedarville, Ohio Virginia Wheaton, Illinois St. Paul, Minnesota California Grand Rapids, Michigan Illinois Michigan Anderson, Indiana Virginia Beach, Virginia Oregon Ohio Trending Companies Wheaton College Palm Beach Atlantic University Regent University Northwestern College Houston Christian University LeTourneau University Samford University Cedarville University Azusa Pacific University Calvin University Trending Categories Faculty Careers - Biology/Life Sciences Faculty Careers - Psychology Faculty Careers - Engineering Education Faculty Careers - Business Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Other Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Development/Fundraising Faculty Careers - Education Faculty Careers - Health Professions Faculty Careers - Religion Faculty Careers - Chemistry/Biochemistry Faculty Careers - Communication/Design/Media Apply for this job Find Jobs By Category Education Faculty Careers - Health Professions Faculty Careers - Biology/Life Sciences Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Other Faculty Careers - Psychology Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Development/Fundraising Faculty Careers - Engineering Faculty Careers - Communication/Design/Media Faculty Careers - Religion Faculty Careers - Chemistry/Biochemistry Powered by Web Scribble Solutions , Inc. About Our Work & Mission Our Institutions Leadership Contact Us Join Us Advertise Donate Employment Membership Sponsorship Follow Us Council for Christian Colleges & Universities 20 M Street SE, Suite 350 , Washington, D.C. 20003 202.546.8713"
