    "https://careers.cccu.org/job/assistant-associate-professor-of-mechanical-engineering-general-cedarville-ohio-12605": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Mechanical Engineering (General)",
      "description": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Mechanical Engineering (General) in Cedarville, Ohio | Council for Christian Colleges and Universities Home Search Directory Contact Us Career Resources Career Advice Interview Coach Offer Analyzer Pricing Register Job Seekers Employers Sign In Post a Job Assistant/Associate Professor of Mechanical Engineering (General) Cedarville University Cedarville, Ohio Share Save Job Apply for This Job Commute Time Show on map From Location To Location 251 N Main St, Cedarville, OH 45314, USA Cedarville University equips Christian undergraduate, graduate, and online students for godly service and vocational distinction. We offer more than 150 programs of study, all from a distinctly biblical worldview. Are you passionate about Mechanical Engineering and the role it plays in shaping and transforming the world we live in? Are you looking to share that passion with a new generation of engineers in a Christ-centered learning environment? If so, then we want to talk to you! The Cedarville University School of Engineering and Computer Science invites applications for an Assistant or Associate Professor of Mechanical Engineering. The Mechanical Engineering Program comprises nine full-time faculty, over three-hundred undergraduate students, and dedicated facilities in areas of manufacturing, rapid prototyping, automotive, and aerospace engineering. Our rigorous program offers rich learning opportunities and cultivates technical professionals who are committed to excellence in character, conduct, and skill. Cedarville University presents a unique faculty opportunity to invest in the lives of students both inside and outside of the classroom, focusing on the development of the whole person in addition to technical training. Faculty candidates are currently sought with expertise in thermal and fluid sciences, aerospace design, experimental methods, or materials engineering. Highly qualified candidates whose expertise lies in other associated areas of mechanical engineering may also be considered. Industry experience in one or more of these areas is considered highly desirable. Given our program’s emphasis on developing applied skills through lab-based and project-based learning, demonstrated experience in practical application and design implementation is strongly preferred . Demonstrated success in educational, mentorship, and training contexts will also be highly regarded. Rank is commensurate with experience and credentials. Eligibility for a tenure-track appointment will be determined based on institutional needs and candidate qualifications at the time of hire. The School of Engineering and Computer Science is housed in a modern facility with extensive state-of-the-art laboratories. We offer ABET-accredited programs in Mechanical Engineering, Civil Engineering, Computer Engineering, Electrical Engineering, and Computer Science (CS), as well as a program in Cyber Operations. Position Responsibilities Teach 24 workload hours (or the equivalent) of undergraduate courses and laboratories per academic year in mechanical engineering. The successful candidate may also be required to teach in other mechanical and general engineering areas as needed for the BSME curriculum and other programs in the school. Demonstrate biblical integration in teaching and mentorship. Guide and mentor senior capstone design projects. Plan and execute laboratory activities, ensuring safe and effective operation of equipment. Support student learning through mentorship, advising, and professional guidance. Advise students in academic, professional, and spiritual development. Contribute to curriculum development, assessment, and accreditation processes (including ABET). Participate in departmental, college, and university service, including committees and outreach initiatives. Maintain professional engagement with the engineering community and foster industry relationships Position Requirements Ph.D. in Mechanical Engineering or related discipline; OR M.S. in Mechanical Engineering (or related discipline) plus licensure as a Professional Engineer (PE); OR M.S. in Mechanical Engineering (or related discipline) plus at least 6 years of professional engineering experience in a relevant area of mechanical engineering. Candidates without a terminal degree but with significant industry experience will be considered. However, they may be required to enroll in further graduate-level studies as a condition of employment. Proven ability to effectively communicate engineering and professional subject matter to students. Strong interpersonal skills and ability to collaborate effectively with colleagues and students. Demonstrated ability to effectively engage in Christian mentorship and discipleship in both one-on-one and larger group contexts. Ability to provide professional mentorship and career guidance. Articulated commitment to and understanding of biblical integration in and out of the classroom. Qualified applicant must be a born-again Christian with a personal commitment to Jesus Christ. Qualified applicant must agree with and be willing to abide by Cedarville University's Doctrinal Statement , Community Covenant , and General Workplace Standards . Employment is subject to the University's verification of credentials along with other information required by law and Cedarville University policies, including the successful completion of a background check. H-1B sponsorship may be available for this position depending upon legal and business considerations. Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. This position, based in Cedarville, Ohio, is pending budget approval. Contact Information For consideration, an employment application must be completed on our online application website. General inquiries: Jennifer Cochran, SHRM-CP, Director of Academic Human Resource Services Position-specific inquiries: Dr. Steve Ayers, Dean, School of Engineering and Computer Science Cedarville University is an Equal Opportunity Employer Job Information Job Category: Faculty Careers - Engineering Education: Doctorate Degree Position Type: Full Time Related Jobs Assistant/Associate Professor of Computer Science Cedarville University Cedarville, Ohio Posted - September 1, 2026 View Nursing - Assistant Professor Hope College Holland, Michigan Posted - September 4, 2026 View Assistant/Associate Professor of History LeTourneau University Longview, Texas Posted - September 3, 2026 View Assistant Professor, Department of Communication and Media (9 Mo, TT) Samford University Birmingham, Alabama Posted - September 3, 2026 View Assistant Professor of Public Relations, Department of Communication and Media (9 Mo, TT) Samford University Birmingham, Alabama Posted - September 3, 2026 View Religion Faculty Calvin University Grand Rapids, Michigan Posted - September 4, 2026 View Show More Jobs Trending Job Titles Nursing Assistant Professor Associate Professor of Finance Trending Locations Anderson, Indiana West Palm Beach, Florida Houston, Texas Alabama Minnesota Florida Grand Rapids, Michigan Wheaton, Illinois ORANGE CITY, Iowa California Azusa, California Michigan Ohio Cedarville, Ohio Virginia Beach, Virginia Illinois Iowa St. Paul, Minnesota Birmingham, Alabama Oregon Virginia Texas Portland, Oregon Longview, Texas Indiana Trending Companies Cedarville University Wheaton College Northwestern College LeTourneau University Palm Beach Atlantic University Houston Christian University Samford University Regent University Calvin University Azusa Pacific University Trending Categories Faculty Careers - Psychology Education Faculty Careers - Chemistry/Biochemistry Faculty Careers - Business Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Other Faculty Careers - Engineering Faculty Careers - Religion Faculty Careers - Education Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Development/Fundraising Faculty Careers - Communication/Design/Media Faculty Careers - Biology/Life Sciences Faculty Careers - Health Professions Apply for this job Find Jobs By Category Education Faculty Careers - Health Professions Faculty Careers - Biology/Life Sciences Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Other Faculty Careers - Psychology Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Development/Fundraising Faculty Careers - Engineering Faculty Careers - Communication/Design/Media Faculty Careers - Religion Faculty Careers - Chemistry/Biochemistry Powered by Web Scribble Solutions , Inc. About Our Work & Mission Our Institutions Leadership Contact Us Join Us Advertise Donate Employment Membership Sponsorship Follow Us Council for Christian Colleges & Universities 20 M Street SE, Suite 350 , Washington, D.C. 20003 202.546.8713"
    },
    "https://careers.cccu.org/job/assistant-associate-professor-of-electrical-engineering-cedarville-ohio-12604": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Electrical Engineering",
      "description": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Electrical Engineering in Cedarville, Ohio | Council for Christian Colleges and Universities Home Search Directory Contact Us Career Resources Career Advice Interview Coach Offer Analyzer Pricing Register Job Seekers Employers Sign In Post a Job Assistant/Associate Professor of Electrical Engineering Cedarville University Cedarville, Ohio Share Save Job Apply for This Job Commute Time Show on map From Location To Location 251 N Main St, Cedarville, OH 45314, USA Cedarville University equips Christian undergraduate, graduate, and online students for godly service and vocational distinction. We offer more than 150 programs of study, all from a distinctly biblical worldview. The Cedarville University School of Engineering and Computer Science is looking for exceptional faculty to join our Electrical Engineering program and help us train outstanding Electrical Engineers who integrate highest level technical skills with an active Christian faith to transform lives across the world. Our program emphasizes rigorous academics combined with extensive hands-on learning and service opportunities. We aim to cultivate technical professionals who are committed to excellence in character, conduct, and skill. Our faculty are dedicated professionals who seek to pour into the lives of our students both in the classroom and beyond. We invite applications for Electrical Engineering faculty opportunities. Appointment is anticipated at the Assistant or Associate Professor level. Rank is commensurate with experience and credentials. Eligibility for a tenure-track appointment will be determined based on institutional needs and candidate qualifications at the time of hire. The School of Engineering and Computer Science offers an ABET-accredited BSCE degree program, in addition to ABET-accredited BSCpE, BSEE, and BSME degrees and BS degrees in Computer Science and Cyber Operations. The school currently has over 750 students across its six primary disciplines. Position Responsibilities: This faculty position primarily focuses on teaching and mentoring students within an undergraduate engineering program. Responsibilities include teaching undergraduate courses and laboratories in a variety of electrical engineering areas, advising students, and advising senior design projects. While school administration will seek to align teaching duties with the candidate’s specific areas of engineering expertise, there may also be a need for the successful candidate to teach in other electrical, computer, and general engineering areas as required for the BSEE curriculum and other programs in the school. The successful candidate will be expected to participate in the continuing development of an innovative curriculum with a strong focus on lab-based learning and project work. Position Requirements: Ph.D. in Electrical Engineering or related discipline; OR M.S. in Electrical Engineering or related discipline, plus at least 6 years of professional engineering experience in a relevant area of electrical engineering. Candidates without a terminal degree may be required to enroll in further graduate-level studies as a condition of employment. Proven ability to effectively communicate engineering and professional subject material to students. Strong interpersonal skills and the ability to work as a team with students and colleagues. Demonstrated ability to effectively engage in Christian mentorship and discipleship in both one-on-one and larger group contexts. Ability to provide professional mentorship and career guidance. Articulated commitment to and understanding of biblical integration in and out of the classroom. Qualified applicant must be a born-again Christian with a personal commitment to Jesus Christ. Qualified applicant must agree with and be willing to abide by Cedarville University's Doctrinal Statement , Community Covenant , General Work Place Standards , and the University’s church membership expectations. Employment is subject to the University's verification of credentials along with other information required by law and Cedarville University policies, including the successful completion of a background check. H-1B sponsorship may be available for this position depending upon legal and business considerations. Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. This position, based in Cedarville, Ohio, is pending budget approval. Contact Information: For consideration, an employment application must be completed on our online application website. All official inquiries should be directed to Jennifer Cochran, SHRM-CP, Director of Academic Human Resource Services. Position-specific inquiries should be directed to Dr. Stephen Ayers, Dean, School of Engineering and Computer Science. Cedarville is an Equal Opportunity Employer Job Information Job Category: Faculty Careers - Engineering Education: Doctorate Degree Position Type: Full Time Related Jobs Assistant/Associate Professor of Computer Science Cedarville University Cedarville, Ohio Posted - September 1, 2026 View Assistant/Associate Professor of Mechanical Engineering (General) Cedarville University Cedarville, Ohio Posted - September 1, 2026 View Assistant Professor, English Department (9 Mo, TT) Samford University Birmingham, Alabama Posted - September 3, 2026 View Assistant/Associate Professor of History LeTourneau University Longview, Texas Posted - September 3, 2026 View Assistant Professor, Department of Communication and Media (9 Mo, TT) Samford University Birmingham, Alabama Posted - September 3, 2026 View Assistant Professor of Public Relations, Department of Communication and Media (9 Mo, TT) Samford University Birmingham, Alabama Posted - September 3, 2026 View Show More Jobs Trending Job Titles Associate Professor of Finance Nursing Assistant Professor Trending Locations ORANGE CITY, Iowa Virginia Portland, Oregon Texas Minnesota Azusa, California Indiana Wheaton, Illinois Cedarville, Ohio Illinois Birmingham, Alabama Virginia Beach, Virginia Florida Houston, Texas Longview, Texas Michigan Alabama Ohio West Palm Beach, Florida California Anderson, Indiana Grand Rapids, Michigan Iowa Oregon St. Paul, Minnesota Trending Companies Northwestern College Regent University Wheaton College Palm Beach Atlantic University Cedarville University Houston Christian University LeTourneau University Azusa Pacific University Samford University Calvin University Trending Categories Faculty Careers - Chemistry/Biochemistry Education Faculty Careers - Religion Faculty Careers - Biology/Life Sciences Faculty Careers - Health Professions Faculty Careers - Education Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Development/Fundraising Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Other Faculty Careers - Engineering Faculty Careers - Business Faculty Careers - Communication/Design/Media Faculty Careers - Psychology Apply for this job Find Jobs By Category Education Faculty Careers - Health Professions Faculty Careers - Biology/Life Sciences Faculty Careers - Business Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Other Faculty Careers - Education Faculty Careers - Psychology Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Development/Fundraising Faculty Careers - Engineering Faculty Careers - Communication/Design/Media Faculty Careers - Religion Faculty Careers - Chemistry/Biochemistry Powered by Web Scribble Solutions , Inc. About Our Work & Mission Our Institutions Leadership Contact Us Join Us Advertise Donate Employment Membership Sponsorship Follow Us Council for Christian Colleges & Universities 20 M Street SE, Suite 350 , Washington, D.C. 20003 202.546.8713"
