    "https://careers.cccu.org/job/registrar-and-director-of-academic-records-houston-texas-12591": {
      "title": "Registrar and Director of Academic Records",
      "description": "Registrar and Director of Academic Records in Houston, Texas | Council for Christian Colleges and Universities Home Search Directory Contact Us Career Resources Career Advice Interview Coach Offer Analyzer Pricing Register Job Seekers Employers Sign In Post a Job Registrar and Director of Academic Records Houston Christian University Houston, Texas Share Save Job Apply for This Job Commute Time Show on map From Location To Location 7502 Fondren Rd, Houston, TX 77074, USA Position Summary: This is a chief administrative position responsible for the operation and development of the Office of Academic Records as a support service to the academic function of the University. Prepares all registration processes, maintains database tables, and oversees online registration. Supports University programs and policies as established by federal, state, administrative, and academic entities. Acts as a central communication resource for academic and policy information related to student records management. Responsible for the maintenance and integrity of academic records. This is a security-sensitive position that reports to the Associate Provost for Academic Affairs. Essential Duties/Responsibilities: Establishes and maintains an organizational structure to effectively accomplish the OAR’s goals and objectives. Sets up all registration tables for online registration, maintains database (Banner SaaS) tables, and oversees registration. Prepares grade sheets and final grades for student access online. Enforces academic rules and regulations; monitors academic standing; coordinates probation, and suspension, as appropriate. Provides technical leadership for Banner Student, Degree Works, and implementation of new software and/or changes to software. VA certification and compliance official. Assists in the coordination of graduation and commencement procedures and ceremonies. Maintains student’s academic records on a permanent basis. Oversees posting student test scores (AP, CLEP, IB and other departmental exams). Recommends and participates in the development and implementation of University policies. Serves as custodian of academic records. Responsible for enrollment and degree reporting to the National Student Clearinghouse. Supervises employees, including participating in hiring and conducting performance evaluations. Develops and processes data reports for the Office of Academic Records and other authorized University personnel. Maintains budgets and budget reports. Serves on committees as requested. Provides professional development, evaluates new technologies, and recommends implementation. Qualification Requirements: Bachelor’s degree required. To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential duty satisfactorily. The requirements listed below are representative of the minimum knowledge, skill, and/or ability required to successfully handle this position. Work to further the University’s mission Must be able to completely affirm, uphold, and live within the Preamble of Houston Christian University and the Ten Pillars Core Convictions Exhibit an active Christian faith with local church membership and involvement Excellent interpersonal and organizational skills Knowledge of, or the ability to learn, University academic policies, procedures, and degree requirements Proficient in the use of Microsoft Office; knowledge of Banner SaaS preferred Monitor changes in the technology sector to discover ways the OAR can improve and develop Excellent analytical and problem solving skills Solid understanding of data analysis Ability to manage a budget and work within the constraints of that budget Ability to communicate effectively in both oral and written form Ability to exercise sound judgment in making critical decisions Ability to establish program goals and objectives that support the strategic plan Ability to supervise others Commitment to providing support for student development and success Experience in data reporting In addition, the successful candidate will be professional, self-reliant, proactive, enthusiastic, and will make a positive impression on others. Job Information Job Category: Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Admissions/ Registrar Education: Bachelor's Degree Position Type: Full Time Related Jobs Vice President of Academic Affairs and Chief Academic Officer Mid-America Christian University - Oklahoma City, OK Oklahoma City, Oklahoma Posted - July 9, 2026 View Transfer Evaluation Analyst Wheaton College Wheaton, Illinois Posted - September 1, 2026 View Director of First Year Experience & Leadership Development Messiah University Mechanicsburg, Pennsylvania Posted - August 26, 2026 View Director of Financial Aid Mid-America Christian University - Oklahoma City, OK Oklahoma City, Oklahoma Posted - July 13, 2026 View Associate Registrar for Records & Student Services Bethel University St. Paul, Minnesota Posted - September 1, 2026 View Vice President Academic and Dean Booth University College Winnipeg, Manitoba, Canada Posted - August 12, 2026 View Show More Jobs Trending Job Titles Associate Professor of Finance Nursing Assistant Professor Trending Locations Grand Rapids, Michigan Iowa Houston, Texas Michigan West Palm Beach, Florida Illinois Wheaton, Illinois Virginia Indiana Birmingham, Alabama St. Paul, Minnesota Florida Cedarville, Ohio Longview, Texas Alabama Oregon Ohio Portland, Oregon California Azusa, California Texas Virginia Beach, Virginia Anderson, Indiana ORANGE CITY, Iowa Minnesota Trending Companies Cedarville University Calvin University Houston Christian University Regent University Palm Beach Atlantic University Azusa Pacific University Samford University LeTourneau University Wheaton College Northwestern College Trending Categories Faculty Careers - Biology/Life Sciences Faculty Careers - Psychology Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Development/Fundraising Faculty Careers - Business Faculty Careers - Religion Faculty Careers - Communication/Design/Media Faculty Careers - Engineering Faculty Careers - Health Professions Faculty Careers - Education Faculty Careers - Chemistry/Biochemistry Education Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Other Apply for this job Find Jobs By Category Education Faculty Careers - Health Professions Faculty Careers - Biology/Life Sciences Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Other Faculty Careers - Psychology Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Development/Fundraising Faculty Careers - Engineering Faculty Careers - Communication/Design/Media Faculty Careers - Religion Faculty Careers - Chemistry/Biochemistry Powered by Web Scribble Solutions , Inc. About Our Work & Mission Our Institutions Leadership Contact Us Join Us Advertise Donate Employment Membership Sponsorship Follow Us Council for Christian Colleges & Universities 20 M Street SE, Suite 350 , Washington, D.C. 20003 202.546.8713"
